The phone/tablet build uses one `:app` APK or AAB and resizes its Compose UI for larger screens. {% if include_wear %}Wear OS is a separate `:wear` APK/AAB with round-screen Compose Material 3, a watch manifest, and a distinct version-code range. The tiny `:core` module shows how to share business logic; extend it with the domain models and services your real app needs. The watch has its own UI because phone layouts and some hardware permissions are unsuitable on a watch. Both packages use `{{ application_id }}` and must use the **same signing key** for companion installs.{% else %}The watch app is omitted. You can add it by rerunning Copier with `include_wear=true` and reviewing the update.{% endif %}

The base app has Material 3, Material 3 Adaptive, lifecycle-aware state, DataStore settings, Coil image loading, Compose tests, and developer tooling. Selected native capability examples live in files such as `NotesDatabase.kt`, `CameraPreview.kt`, or `LanDiscovery.kt` and are intentionally not launched before the app asks for relevant permissions.

### Visual design

The Copier-selected `{{ visual_style }}` style controls the phone/tablet app's Material 3 typography, colors, corner radii and starter components. `native` follows refined system typography and supports Android dynamic colors by default; `editorial` uses serif headings and warm, paper-like surfaces; `technical` emphasizes large monospace metrics, a cool palette and fine outlines. All three support light, dark, AMOLED and optional system dynamic colors. They are **starting points**, not dependencies on bundled fonts or a separate UI framework.

Use `AppSpace` for spacing, `MaterialTheme.typography` for text, `MaterialTheme.shapes` for corners, and `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` for color. Reuse `AppSectionHeading` and `AppInfoCard` in `UiComponents.kt`; extend these tokens as your app develops. The watch uses its own round-screen Wear Material 3 theme and is not restyled by the phone preset.

{% if 'algolia' in ui_addons %}Algolia InstantSearch is linked, but search requires your own Algolia app ID, index, and search-only API key. Keep administrative credentials off-device.
