## Release artifacts

```sh
task release:phone    # app/build/outputs/apk|bundle/release
{% if include_wear %}task release:wear     # wear/build/outputs/apk|bundle/release
{% endif %}task release          # all selected targets
```

The manual **Build release artifacts** GitHub Action packages APKs and AABs for download. Distribution and store publishing are outside this template's scope. Without signing credentials, release outputs are unsigned and not ready for distribution. For signing locally, set `ANDROID_SIGNING_STORE_FILE`, `ANDROID_SIGNING_STORE_PASSWORD`, `ANDROID_SIGNING_KEY_ALIAS`, `ANDROID_SIGNING_KEY_PASSWORD`. For GitHub Actions, create the equivalent three password/alias secrets plus `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64` containing the base64-encoded keystore. Never commit a keystore or secrets. Increase `app.versionCode` and `app.versionName` in `gradle.properties` before each release. {% if include_wear %}The Wear build offsets its version code by 100000 to distinguish phone and watch artifacts; keep the base version below 100000.{% endif %}

Start with one feature, get it running on the emulator, and expand the capability selection only when it is useful. A watch companion is not automatically equivalent to every phone feature; file access, scanner, LAN and media features need device-specific permission and UI testing.
